   "design": "With the patient's consent, a certified scribe drafts the clinical note and each visit note from the recorded consultation, and the orthodontist corrects every draft before it is saved. Patients fill in the medical history online before the first visit, so it loads into the record instead of being copied from paper. Imaging and scanner software store images straight into the patient record. Each visit type in the note maps to its billing code by fixed rules, which the orthodontist checks. Photos, landmarks, the examination and the treatment plan stay with the orthodontist.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Notes were typed after each patient and histories copied from paper.",
   "enabler_now": "Certified scribes, online questionnaires and imaging integration.",
   "still_hard": "Patients who refuse recording.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing the face, not only the teeth.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less typing and copying; diagnosis stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "patient",
     "task": "Share history",
     "learn": "Whether the first visit is shorter."
    }
   ],
